From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quentin Casasnovas <quentin.casasnovas@vates.tech>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 17:08:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bnx2x: use kernel definition of BITS_TO_BYTES when available.

The kernel has its own definition since 1ce62f5178e4 ("ocfs2/dlm: move
BITS_TO_BYTES() to bitops.h for wider use") in v4.19.285.

Signed-off-by: Quentin Casasnovas <quentin.casasnovas@vates.tech>
---
 bnx2x-1.715.8/src/bnx2x_init.h | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bnx2x-1.715.8/src/bnx2x_init.h b/bnx2x-1.715.8/src/bnx2x_init.h
index 847a6bc42823..86a7310b8601 100644
--- a/bnx2x-1.715.8/src/bnx2x_init.h
+++ b/bnx2x-1.715.8/src/bnx2x_init.h
@@ -308,7 +308,9 @@ static inline void bnx2x_dcb_config_qm(struct bnx2x *bp, enum cos_mode mode,
  *    possible, the driver should only write the valid vnics into the internal
  *    ram according to the appropriate port mode.
  */
+#ifndef BITS_TO_BYTES
 #define BITS_TO_BYTES(x) ((x)/8)
+#endif
 
 /* CMNG constants, as derived from system spec calculations */
 
